  "title": "Bugfix/unused const error with old gcrypt",
  "description": "Not sure if that's the proper way to contribute, but I haven't found contributing documentation, so here it goes.\n\n#### The bug:\nSeveral dissectors contain `#if`s on gcrypt version and features.\nWhen compiling with old version of gcrypt (<1.6.0), those `#if`s leave some `static const` variables unused.\nThis in turn emits a warning (`-Wunused-const`) which makes `-Werror` fail the build.\n##### How to reproduce: compile with gcrypt<1.6.0 (found on centos7 for example).\n\n#### The solution:\nMove those const declarations inside a corresponding `#if`.\n\nWhy this bothers me: I compile wireshark on my centos7 machine, which has libgcrypt 1.5.2.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2020-08-24T08:07:37.306Z",
